  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1204 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nAbove normal temperatures will continue through the rest of the week \nwith a generally stagnant synoptic pattern persisting. Most models \ncontinue to indicate a weak rex-type block developing over the \nsouthern plains states during this time, which will consequently \nfavor dry weather as tropical moisture is confined well to our \nsouth. Highs in the 80s look likely each day, and while this is \nseveral degrees above average, we expect to remain well below record \nvalues. This weekend, model consensus favors a return to a more \namplified upper level pattern as deep troughing develops over the \nwestern CONUS. This could result in a return of better moisture \ncourtesy of southwest flow aloft, but for now a dry forecast is \nfavored. The more noticable impact with this pattern change will be \nyet another warm-up with highs in the mid 80s to lower 90s through \nearly next week.",
